// Island Birth: phase changes that build land.
//
// Night on a basalt sea coast. A glowing feeder dyke climbs the cliff and
// feeds a lava river along the rim, which shoots out over the edge in a jet
// and breaks into three falls that drop 22 m into a cold (15 C) sea. Lava
// holds liquid on its 250 C latent-heat plateau, but a falling liquid that
// freezes becomes its solid's debris: below a chill band halfway down, most of
// each fall freezes in flight and lands as glowing cinders (rubble), while a
// thin core lands as liquid lava. Water touching lava reacts into obsidian
// and steam. The cinders pile up on the shallow shelf at the cliff foot,
// break the surface by 10 s as three glowing cones, merge into one ridge and
// keep climbing into a headland. Colour follows temperature: the falls are
// yellow-white, the fresh cone tops orange, the flanks dull red, the
// waterline black. Hot air shimmers over the falls and the new rock.
//
// Steam (density -10, cooling 5) boils off the waterline at the cones, rises
// through the hot air, bends downwind with wind 2, and condenses at 90 C; a
// light drizzle falls on the seaward flank. Mist sources on the open sea lay a
// low haze downwind. At 31 s the falls thin out from the far end and stop,
// the river crusts over, and the sea quenches the new land from the
// waterline upward in an uneven front, leaving it black with a glowing summit
// as the camera pulls back.
//
// The temperatures that set the look are scripted with `temp` events: the air
// around the falls is held at 1290 C (which keeps the jet liquid and makes the
// heat haze), the chill band at 450 C and then a cinder band whose
// temperature drops over the run (840, 680, 560, 500, then 680 C for the last
// summit cinders), and the final quench front at 400 C.
[scene]
name = island birth
description = A lava river on a night sea cliff shoots out over the rim and breaks into three falls; cinders that freeze in flight pile into three glowing cones that rise out of the cold sea and merge into a new headland, steam drifts downwind, and the land cools black from the waterline up while its summit still glows.
size = 1280 720
seed = 0x15b1
wind = 2
ticks = 2280

[build]
// Bedrock floor, sea, and the deep seabed.
fill 0 700 1280 720 bedrock
fill 380 470 1280 700 water
terrain 610 1280 612 14 70 sand 700
